<report>
<line><title>Risk analysis (retrospective)</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><th></th><tdfirst><subtotal>Characteristic factor:</subtotal></tdfirst><td></td></tr>
<tr><td><subtotal>Outcome:</subtotal></td><td>Present</td><td>Absent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Positive</td><td><in>aa</in></td><td><in>bb</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Negative</td><td><in>cc</in></td><td><in>dd</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Observed odds ratio = <in>odds</in></line>
<line>Approximate power <in>pwr</in></line>
<block name="power">
<line></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Woolf, logit) <in>ci</in>% confidence interval = <in>ci_1</in>  to  <in>ci_2</in> </ci></line>
<line></line>
</block>
<line>Conditional maximum likelihood estimates:</line>
<line>Conditional estimate of odds ratio = <in>eor</in></line>
<line><ci>Exact Fisher <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llf</in>  to  <in>ulf</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact Fisher one sided <in>p1f</in>, two sided <in>p2f</in></pval></line>
<line><ci>Exact mid-P <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>llm</in>  to  <in>ulm</in></ci></line>
<line><pval>Exact mid-P one sided <in>p1m</in>, two sided <in>p2m</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<block name="risk">
<line>Population exposure % = <in>pe</in></line>
<line>Population attributable risk % = <in>par</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from</in>  to  <in>to</in></ci></line>
</block>
</report>